Task: Deploy a Python Application on EKS


Architecture


    Developer
        |
        v
    GitHub
        |
        v
    Docker Image
        |
        v
    Amazon ECR
        |
        v
    Amazon EKS
        |
        +--> Deployment
        |
        +--> Service
        |
        +--> Ingress (ALB)


Task 1: Create EKS Cluster

    Create Cluster


        eksctl create cluster \
        --name dev-cluster \
        --region ap-south-1 \
        --nodegroup-name workers \
        --node-type t3.medium \
        --nodes 2

    Verify:

        kubectl get nodes


Task 2: Create ECR Repository

    aws ecr create-repository \
        --repository-name flask-app

    List:

        aws ecr describe-repositories


Task 3: Create Python App

    app.py

        from flask import Flask

        app = Flask(__name__)

        @app.route("/")
        def home():
            return "Hello from EKS"

        app.run(host="0.0.0.0", port=5000)

Task 4: Dockerize Application

    Dockerfile

    FROM python:3.12-slim

    WORKDIR /app

    COPY . .

    RUN pip install -r requirements.txt

    EXPOSE 5000

    CMD ["python","app.py"]

    
    Build:

        docker build -t flask-app .

    Run locally:

        docker run -p 5000:5000 flask-app


Task 5: Push Image to ECR

    Login:

        aws ecr get-login-password \
        | docker login \
        --username AWS \
        --password-stdin ACCOUNT_ID.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com

    Tag:

        docker tag flask-app:latest \
        ACCOUNT_ID.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/flask-app:v1

    Push:

        docker push \
        ACCOUNT_ID.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/flask-app:v1


Task 6: Create Namespace

    kubectl create ns dev

Verify:

    kubectl get ns





